133	Read before you settle: run the `sync` and `sdd-dir` steps below and read
134	the ledger's plan line, if the ledger exists (reading it changes nothing).
135	Then settle where the work happens: use hyperpowers:using-git-worktrees,
136	which detects an existing worktree or asks your human partner to choose
137	between staying on the current branch, a new branch in place, and a
138	worktree, and reports the mode. When the plan line names an integration
139	branch, this is a later session of a running plan: hand using-git-worktrees
140	that branch and your session id. Never start implementation on a main/master
141	branch unless your human partner chose "stay on the current branch" in that
142	question; that answer is the consent, and the dossier no longer depends on
143	the branch.
144	
145	Conversation memory does not survive compaction. In real sessions,
146	controllers that lost their place have re-dispatched entire completed task
147	sequences — the single most expensive failure observed. Track progress in
148	a ledger file, not only in todos.
149	
150	- Each plan owns a workspace: at skill start, run `scripts/sdd-state sync PLAN_FILE`
151	  (it fetches the repository's state branch; outcomes below), then this
152	  skill's `scripts/sdd-dir PLAN_FILE` — it prints the plan's workspace
153	  inside the repository's state checkout under the user cache
154	  (`${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/hyperpowers/state/<key>/plans/<plan-slug>-<hash8>/`,
155	  one checkout per clone, shared by every worktree of it), home to every
156	  artifact for THIS plan: ledger, briefs, reports, review packages, claims,
157	  tier-skip summary. The ledger, reports, notes and claims are committed to
158	  the orphan branch `hyperpowers/state` by `scripts/sdd-state snapshot PLAN_FILE`
159	  and travel between hosts with that branch; briefs and review packages are
160	  ignored there and regenerate. The cache is off any protected path, so
161	  writing there never triggers a permission prompt, and it is outside the
162	  working tree, so it can never be committed with the code. Another plan's
163	  directory is never yours to read or write. When `sdd-dir` reports
164	  `backend=plain` on stderr, the state branch is unavailable on this host
165	  and the dossier will not travel from it: tell your human partner once and
166	  continue.
167	- `sdd-state sync` outcomes: `up-to-date`, `fast-forwarded`, `merged`,
168	  `ahead`, `created`, `absent`, `no-remote`, `assumed-absent`, `plain`:
169	  continue. `offline` (exit 1): continue on the local checkout and, as soon
170	  as the ledger exists (the next bullet), append
